{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[\\dfrac{10}{3x^3}\\right]$ is the *second derivative* of $\\dfrac{10}{3x^3}$.\n\nIn other words, it's the derivative of $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{10}{3x^3}\\right]$, which is the derivative of $\\dfrac{10}{3x^3}$.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[\\dfrac{10}{3x^3}\\right]$, we need to differentiate $\\dfrac{10}{3x^3}$ twice.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's start by finding $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{10}{3x^3}\\right]$:\n\n$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{10}{3x^3}\\right]=-\\dfrac{10}{x^4}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{10}{3x^3}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{10}{3}\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{1}{x^3}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{10}{3}\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[x^{-3}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{10}{3}\\left(-3x^{-4}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-10x^{-4}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{10}{x^4}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\left(\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\right)\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{2}\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{1}{2}\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Now we can differentiate $-\\dfrac{10}{x^4}$ to find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[\\dfrac{10}{3x^3}\\right]$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[\\dfrac{10}{3x^3}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-\\dfrac{10}{x^4}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{40}{x^5}\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[\\dfrac{10}{3x^3}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-\\dfrac{10}{x^4}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-10\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[x^{-4}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-10\\left(-4x^{-5}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=40x^{-5}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{40}{x^5}\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[\\dfrac{10}{3x^3}\\right]=\\dfrac{40}{x^5}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[\\dfrac{10}{3x^3}\\right]$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{40}{x^5}$","correct":true},{"content":"$-\\dfrac{10}{x^4}$","correct":false},{"content":"$-\\dfrac{5}{9x^5}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{10}{3x^2}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
